title: "Applied Machine Learning in Python: A Hands-on Guide with Code"

message: >
  If you use this book, software, or educational materials in your
  research or teaching, please cite it using the metadata below.

type: book

authors:
  - family-names: "Pyrcz"
    given-names: "Michael J."
    affiliation: "The University of Texas at Austin"
    orcid: "0000-0002-5983-219X"

abstract: >
  An open-source, hands-on guide to applied machine learning using Python.
  The book integrates machine learning concepts with practical examples,
  interactive Jupyter notebooks, and reproducible workflows. Topics include
  data analytics, supervised and unsupervised learning, regression,
  classification, dimensionality reduction, neural networks, deep learning,
  time series analysis, and machine learning applications in engineering
  and geoscience. Supporting materials include a comprehensive glossary,
  YouTube lecture series, GitHub repositories, and interactive computational
  dashboards.

